1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,731
Fourteen years had passed.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,672
Fourteen years of exile, sacrifice, pain... and an unwavering promise.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,952
But tonight, Ayodhya was waiting for its king.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,553
After defeating Ravana and fulfilling his destiny,

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,381
Lord Ram began his journey home,

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,876
accompanied by Sita and Lakshman.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,368
When the people heard that Ram was returning,

8
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,214
the entire kingdom prepared to welcome him.

9
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:31,447
Every home became a place of celebration.

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,942
But the diya was more than a lamp.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,583
It represented the light of knowledge,

12
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:39,194
the strength of hope,

13
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,697
and the victory of good over evil.

14
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,492
And then, the moment Ayodhya had waited for finally arrived.

15
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,945
Their beloved Ram had returned.

16
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,843
One lamp became thousands.

17
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,076
Darkness surrendered to light.

18
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:03,543
And Ayodhya transformed into a celebration that would live for generations.

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,792
It was not merely the return of a king.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,330
It was the reunion of a family, the fulfillment of a promise,

21
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:14,809
and the restoration of righteousness.

22
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,205
That is why Diwali is more than a celebration.

23
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,842
It reminds us that even after the longest darkness,

24
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:26,273
truth, courage and dharma can guide us towards light.

25
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,585
Light is not just something we place outside our homes.

26
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,342
It is something we must keep alive within ourselves.

27
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:40,511
From that legendary night, the lights of Diwali became a timeless reminder:

28
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,638
darkness may surround us, but it never has to define us.

29
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,406
May the light of Shri Ram illuminate every heart.

30
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:53,894
Wishing you and your family a blessed Badi Diwali.

31
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:56,009
Jai Shri Ram.
